  "worked_solution": "The power set of $A,$ denoted $P(A),$ is the set that contains every possible subset of $A,$ including the empty set $∅.$\n\nSo, let's list all possible subsets of $A$ using a tree diagram.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/multivariable/14180007/assets/05aba1d74ce21be5c12c7f72b0e5e9f5862b2a8ee67436f18fad1da1542bbc11.png)\n\nAccording to our diagram, the subsets of $A$ are\n\n$$\n∅=\\{\\},\\,\\{\\{∅\\}\\},\\,\\{4\\},\\,\\{4,\\{∅\\}\\}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have \n\n$$\nP(A)=\\{∅,\\{4\\},\\{\\{∅\\}\\},\\{4,\\{∅\\}\\}\\}.\n$$",
